      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-12-12_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>LEAST MONEY AT</head>
        <p>LEAST MONEY AT</p>
        <p>ALF. TAYLOR'S,</p>
        <p>45, HORSEMARKET-STRERT, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>CASH BOOT STORE</p>
        <p>FAIR WEAR OR A NEW PAIR.</p>
        <p>GRANTHAM INDUSTRIAL and FINE ART EXHIBITION, Janußry 20-21 and 22, 19.)41.</p>
        <p>J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk. eOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.—THE MOTOR CAR ACT. 1993. 2/114 MOTOR CAR (REGISTRATION AND LICENSING) ORDER, 1903. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN th..t Motor Cars and Motor 01es required to be registered under the above Act may ue reglstered at the office of the Chief Constable at the Polce Drell:llse. in Arolev-street. APPlications for Licenses for drivers of motor cars anti 'Motor cycles must be made to the Chief Constable. gjeorms of apolication can be obtained at the Town Clerk's ce or at the office of the Chief Constable. bated this 27th day of November. 1903. 3. LYON WHITTLE, Town Cleric, 2i3vril Hell. Warrington.</p>
        <p>COUNTY Bt )110UO II OP WAR NINOTON.— THE lIMPLOYVIENT OP CHILDREN ACT. 1903. NOTICE I HEREBY GIVEN, that on the 15t day of JANUARY, 1904. the following general Restrictions on Employment of Children will come in force : SECTION 3.-0.1 A child (i.e.. a person under the age of 14' shall not be employed between the hours o Nine in the evening and Six in the morning Provided that any local authority mar. by byelaw. vary these hours either generally or for any specified occupation. (2.1 A child under the age of ELEVEN years shall not be employed in STREET TR &amp;PIRG. (3.) No 'child who is employed half-time under the Paetory and Workshop Act, 1901, shall be employed in any other eccupotion. (4.) A child !hall not be employe Ito lift, carry,or move anything so heavy as to be likely to cause injury to the cbild. (5.1 A child shall not he employed in any occupation likely to be injurious to his lite, limb, health or educa- tion, regard tieing had to his physical condition. Until the Town Council as the Local Authority mak,bye laws varying the hours of employment under section 3 (1) the aboYe general restriction will he in force. No Boy or Girl under the age of 14 years may be employed contrary to such restriction, for instance in selling or delivering milk or newspapers or other asticles, carrying parcels, trading In the streets, or be employed in any glop or other premises or in any industrial work at home. The penalty for the first offence is a fine not exceeding 401. and in the case of a second or subsegnent offence not exceeding £5. The person who commits the offence whether he he the employer, agent or workman or the parent or guardian will be Italie to the penalty. Dated this 11th day of Deeember, 1903. J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk, Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
