      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-12-12_WidnesExaminer_art0014" n="art0014">
        <head>FASHIONS OF TO-DAY.</head>
        <p>FASHIONS OF TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>We are apt to call Madame la Mode a dame of capricious fancies, but vhen on(</p>
        <p>conies to</p>
        <p>consider the revolutions of the fashion it is borne home on the mind that idea is altogether erroneous, and that she is instead an individual who insists on the regular re-appearance of certain styles of dress. The pity is that • she is apt to fly, to extremes (a failing of femininity generally) and fall into the error of exaggerating the styles which when less pronounced were in themselves pretty and artistic. in this way the threatened evolution of the crinoline proper from the full skirts worn disturbed the world of dress and agitated it to its core, but</p>
        <p>wheel of</p>
