        <p>The Norfolk village of Great Hockham, which has ti population of only some 500 souls, claim somewhat of a record in the matter of old people. Eleven of them total 899 years, or an average of over 81, and all are in full possession of their faculties and none are bed- ridden.</p>
        <p>Anunusual occurrence is reported from Fenton, one of the Pottery towns. To tipping a load of shrafY from a cart into a disused marl-hole the youth in charge of the vehicle backed the horse too far, and both animal and cart fell to the bottom. There Nyasa- large quantity of water in the hole as the result of the recent rains, and the horse was drowned.</p>
