        <p>WIDNES v. HULL KINGSTON ROVERS. At Widnes.—A dense Ayr prevailed,and at times from the ring side it was difficult to follow the progress of the game. The home team had the best of the first half , and Waiting scored a try,which was not improved upon. I Theseconehalf was evenly contested, no further scor- ing taking place, and the game ended in a win for Widnes by one try (three paints) to nothing. . LANCASHIRE COMBINATION. WIGAN "A" v. WARRINGTON •'A.",. These teams met at Wigan on Saturday when War- rington sustained a defeat. A dense fog prevailed, and the play was followed with difficulty. Wigan pressed at the outset,and Green scored after ten minutes' play. The game went even after this for a long period, until a few minutes before the interval, wlrpn Healey got away, and passing to Green, this speedy player regis- tered his second try. In the second half the game was of a give-and-take nature. From a cross-kick Green scoredat the corner, and the goal kick being a failure, the final score read: Wigan, three tries (nine points) ; Warrington, two tries (six Obits). INTER-WORKS LEAGUE. -- WALKER'S v. CRO•iFIELD's. This match was played on Saturday, and resulted in a win for 'Walker's by 8 points to 3 pints. Rylands v. Cable and L. and N. v. N tylor's can- celled.</p>
